leds: flash: leds-qcom-flash: Fix two problems unbinding the driver

Two bugs from the driver's first version, both found by unbinding it with
lockdep and kmemleak on: the mutex goes before the LEDs do, and the loop
releasing the V4L2 flash devices misses all of them when there's one LED.

Both were tested on a PMI632, on a Moto G Power (2021), with a patch this
series doesn't include that adds that PMIC to the driver. On plain v7.4-rc1
they are only compile tested. Nothing here touches what the PMI632 patch
adds, and they don't depend on it.
